  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at Liberty Hall in Lawrence, Kansas, on Saturday, September 18, 2021, delivering a two-hour set that spans their extensive catalog [1][2]. This recording, taped and transferred by Liz Hamilton, captures twenty-two songs including a four-song encore [1]. The setlist features a mix of recent and deep-cut material, beginning with “Treetop Song” from *New Asian Cinema* and “Wild Sage” from *Get Lonely* [1]. Notable archival rarities include “Calling Out Your Name,” a Rich Mullins cover, and “Etruscans” from *Our First 100 Days*, which is the only archived performance of that track [1][2]. The band also played “Collapsing Stars” from the *Dilaudid EP* and “1 Samuel 15:23” from *The Life of the World to Come* [1]. Tracks from *Transcendental Youth* such as “Until I Am Whole” and “The Diaz Brothers” appear alongside *The Sunset Tree* staples like “Dance Music” and “You or Your Memory” [1]. The performance moves through *Beat the Champ* and *Tallahassee* material before closing with *We Shall All Be Healed* and *The Sunset Tree* tracks [1]. The encore revisits *Beat the Champ* with “Southwestern Territory” and concludes with “Love Cuts the Strings,” “No Children,” and “This Year” [1]. As the 321st archived show for the band, this recording follows a performance at the Tower Theatre the previous day [2].",
